# /titans — Pre-Olympian Registry

The Titans are the processing layer that existed before the Olympian gods.  
In the GAIA system they sit between raw field oscillation and the Pantheon pipeline.

---

## Architecture

```
gaia.html
  └── import from titans/index.js
        ├── kronos.js      (extract from gaia.html — inline for now)
        ├── hyperion.js    ✦ ACTIVE
        ├── rhea.js        ○ planned
        ├── oceanus.js     ○ planned
        ├── themis.js      ○ planned
        ├── mnemosyne.js   ○ planned
        ├── prometheus.js  ○ planned
        └── iapetus.js     ○ planned
```

## Pipeline Order

Data flows through Titans before reaching the Olympians:

```
Raw Field (Kairos ↔ Apollo phase engine)
    ↓
KRONOS    — Phase accumulation, time-as-oscillation
    ↓
HYPERION  — Signal amplification, noise suppression
    ↓
[RHEA]    — Rhythm regulation, flow smoothing
    ↓
[OCEANUS] — Deep data streaming, persistence prep
    ↓
[THEMIS]  — Threshold law, gate decisions
    ↓
[MNEMOSYNE] — Memory write, context packaging
    ↓
[PROMETHEUS] — LLM fire gate (Apollo/Claude handoff)
    ↓
APOLLO    — Synthesis, archetype interpretation
```

## Module Contract

Each Titan module exports a named object with:

| Export         | Type       | Status     | Description                        |
|----------------|------------|------------|------------------------------------|
| `lore`         | object     | ✦ all      | Mythic text strings by state       |
| `draw()`       | function   | ○ phase 2  | Canvas renderer                    |
| `update()`     | function   | ○ phase 2  | Physics / math tick                |
| `config`       | object     | ○ phase 2  | Default params                     |
| `schema`       | object     | ✦ hyperion | DB column definitions + SQL        |
| `archetypes`   | object     | ✦ hyperion | State → archetype mapping          |

## Adding a New Titan

1. Create `titans/<name>.js` following the `hyperion.js` pattern
2. Uncomment its export in `titans/index.js`
3. Add it to `TITAN_PIPELINE` array in `titans/index.js`
4. **Do not modify `gaia.html`** — import the module and mount it

## GaiaDB

Titan states write to the `titan_states` table.  
Each Titan carries a `schema` export with the SQL to extend that table  
when it is promoted from lore-only to a full active agent.

Run `hyperion.schema.sql` to add Hyperion columns when ready.
